/var/adm/messages file.
=A0
2) Tried the command: #logger -p user.debug "testing...", and found that =
this sends the message "tacrib1 root: testing...", both to CW and also =
to the /var/adm/message file. This shows that the connections are there =
from logger to user.debug through the serial console and also to the =
messages file.
=A0
3) Added auth.debug=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 /dev/console to syslog.conf, but =
still not working (even after killing syslogd and restarting it using =
/sbin/rc3.d/S09syslog start, then verified syslog process restarted). =
However, auth.log and user.log get written to correctly, by using the =
'logger -p ' test above.
=A0
4) Verified that the lpr.info writes to syslog lpr.log correctly by =
generating a print job to taclsr that failed.
=A0=A0=A0 "more /etc/syslog.conf | lpr -P taclsr3"
